// EINT0 on a BridgeZone, STANDALONE -- not loaded after pins.csp.
//
// Few enough names to fit one string segment, which is the point while the
// segment/rom_nn question is open: with pins.csp the image needs two, and
// everything past the first was read out of empty RAM.
//
// P0.16 is the AVR's wakeup line (LPC_WAKEUP in the old cfg.h), muxed to eint0
// by the board file. On an LPC2000 a pin interrupt IS a pin function -- there is
// no GPIO interrupt block, that arrived with the 17xx -- so that mux is what
// makes this reach the EINT at all.
//
// FALLING ONLY. EXTPOLAR picks one direction, so `both` is refused on this part
// rather than guessed at.
#digital Wake in falling 0:16

// AND ONE YOU CAN REACH. P0.16 goes to the AVR; P0.30 is Ain4 on a screw
// terminal and carries eint3 on function 2, muxed there by the board file --
// which costs Ain4 as an analog input for as long as that line is in.
//
// An analog input has a divider and usually a filter in front of it, so the
// edge is slow. A slow edge through a logic threshold can trip several times on
// the way -- more counts than pulls is the interrupt seeing what a 500 Hz read
// does not.
#digital Term in falling 0:30

// Can1Yellow. Active high: the pin drives a MOSFET gate with a 10k pulldown.
#digital Lamp out 0:19

#variable Edges = 0

#when Wake.fired
  Edges = Edges + 1
  println("wake ", Edges, " level=", Wake)
#end

#when Term.fired
  Edges = Edges + 1
  println("term ", Edges, " level=", Term)
#end

Lamp = Term
